          </div>
        </form>
        <div class="instructions">
          <h2>Clipping Instructions</h2>
          <a href="#" class="close" rel='nofollow'><i class="icon-cancel-circle"></i></a>
          <p>There are three ways to set in and out points for a clip:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Slide the yellow markers on the progress bar to your desired points</li>
            <li>Enter the times in the "Start Time" or "End Time" text boxes</li>
            <li>Find your point and click "Set start/end at video time" under the "Start Time" or "End Time" text boxes</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Check your selection with the "Preview Clip" option</p>
          <p>If satisfied,</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Enter the title and description of the clip</li>
            <li>Click "Save Clip"</li>
          </ul>
          <p>If you are editing the times of an existing clip, you may only set a start and end time within the original clip boundaries</p>
        </div>
